{"uid":"bb7b4d66a71e313b","name":"test_review_post_rejection_tail_exhausts_max_approaches_to_the_exhausted_hold","fullName":"tests.test_deadline#test_review_post_rejection_tail_exhausts_max_approaches_to_the_exhausted_hold","historyId":"54f404bcf5e05285b0c1465cc233b6bc","time":{"start":1791980415873,"stop":1791980415968,"duration":95},"description":"`_step_review`'s post-rejection twin (docstring site 2): an\n    ordinary, bare-reason rejection (no findings.json written, so none of\n    the curable/incurable/repeated-signature/ruled branches above the\n    bottom tail ever fire) on the LAST approach, with the park disabled,\n    resolves as an unanswered park (v0.36 requirement B) that holds the run\n    `exhausted` (`exhaustedBudget: approaches`) instead of ending it\n    `failed`; driven through a real `run_job()` over\n    `make_supervisor` (never this run's own directory) -- the in-process\n    sibling of `tests/flows/test_flow_review_replan_pause.py::test_a_\n    rejection_on_the_last_approach_with_nothing_curable_fails`, which\n    already pins the same edge end to end over a real engine subprocess;\n    this node additionally asserts the C.1 flag directly, which that flow\n    test (reading only `state`/`verdict`) does not.","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>_step_review</code>'s post-rejection twin (docstring site 2): an<br />\nordinary, bare-reason rejection (no findings.json written, so none of<br />\nthe curable/incurable/repeated-signature/ruled branches above the<br />\nbottom tail ever fire) on the LAST approach, with the park disabled,<br />\nresolves as an unanswered park (v0.36 requirement B) that holds the run<br />\n<code>exhausted</code> (<code>exhaustedBudget: approaches</code>) instead of ending it<br />\n<code>failed</code>; driven through a real <code>run_job()</code> over<br />\n<code>make_supervisor</code> (never this run's own directory) -- the in-process<br />\nsibling of <code>tests/flows/test_flow_review_replan_pause.py::test_a_ rejection_on_